description = "Expose data to be polled by Modbus clients (masters).  This supports TCP, Serial, and RTU communication layers.  It also provides conversion functions to manipulate register data to/from Modbus into data types other than U16.  It supports conversion to/from 16, 32, 64 bit signed and unsigned integers and to/from float32 and double formats.  \0A\0AIt assumes all registers on the device follow the modbus standard (big endian U16) but supports flexibility for endian format of words for multi-register data elements.  \0A\0AConfiguration uses a CSV format to specify channels, directions, and conversions and expects CSV with the following format:\0A\0AChannel Name:  Should contain name using letters, numbers, -, and _\0A\0AStart Address (0 base).  The starting (lowest) address for the modbus registers.  Data that uses more than 16 bits (eg U32 or Doubles) will automatically read/write multiple addresses.  Register values are 0 based (some devices document registers starting at 1). The value should be in hex format.  A hex prefix of 0x is optional.  \0A\0AModbus Function:  There is no default value and if no match is found it will provide a warning.  Valid functions are:\0A- R_Coil (Read Coil)\0A- R_HoldReg (Read Holding Register)\0A- R_DI (Read Discrete Input)\0A- R_InReg (Read Input Register)\0A- W_Coil (Write Coil)\0A- W_HoldReg (Write Holding Register)\0A- W_DI (Write Discrete Input, server/slave only)\0A- W_InReg (Write Input Register, server/slave only)\0A\0AData type: This is only used for registers and is ignored for coil or discrete input operations.  For register R/W the data will be reformated to/from this type. The data type will also control how many registers are read/written.  Valid options are:\0A- U16 (default)\0A- I16\0A- U32\0A- I32\0A- U64\0A- I64\0A- Float32\0A- Double\0A\0AEndian Word:  This is only used for data types that span multiple modbus registers.  Modbus specifies data in a register is big endian but does not specify how values that span multiple registers are managed.  This defines the endian of the registers (at a word level).  Valid options are:\0A- BE_Word (Big Endian Word, default)\0A- LE_Word (Little Endian Word)"
